 "text": "The marathon is named after a battle, and its famous story probably never happened. 490 BC, Greece. A huge Persian army lands at Marathon near Athens. Athens sends a runner, Pheidippides, to Sparta to ask for help. The Athenians win the battle. Centuries later, writers add a dramatic twist. A runner races from Marathon to Athens, announces the victory, and drops dead. The oldest account, by Herodotus, never mentions that run. In 1879, a poem makes the legend famous. Rejoice, we conquer! Then a French scholar, Michel Brial, suggests a race from Marathon to Athens for the first modern Olympics in 1896. A battle legend that became the most famous race on earth. Every legend has a beginning.",
